### Clients — create and fetch.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@apiKey = dev-only-insecure-key-do-not-use-in-production-env

### Create a client. Expect 201 with a Location header.
# first_name, last_name and email are required; description and social_links are not.
# Email is unique, so sending this a second time returns 409. Change the address
# to run it again, or reset the corpus with `docker compose down -v && docker compose up -d`.
# JetBrains users: copy the id from this response into @clientId below.
# @name createClient
POST {{baseUrl}}/clients
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "first_name": "Ada",
  "last_name": "Lovelace",
  "email": "ada.lovelace@analytical.example",
  "description": "Mathematician consolidating two pensions, interested in annuity structures.",
  "social_links": [
    "https://www.linkedin.com/in/ada-lovelace",
    "https://www.linkedin.com/company/analytical-engines"
  ]
}

### The id of the client created above, for the requests that follow.
@clientId = {{createClient.response.body.$.id}}

### Fetch it back. Expect 200.
GET {{baseUrl}}/clients/{{clientId}}
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### The new client is searchable by name.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=Lovelace
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### And by a company in a social link, which no name or email contains.
# word_similarity scores the link text, so this is an identity-tier hit.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=analytical-engines
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### A description hit is weaker evidence, so it ranks below documents (context tier).
# "annuity structures" appears only in the description above.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=annuity%20structures
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}

### Typo tolerance: trigram matching still finds Mary Henderson from a misspelling.
# "Hendersen" scores 0.70, just above the 0.6 lexical floor.
GET {{baseUrl}}/search?q=Hendersen
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
